{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f77e39d99b57bc5b73", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Chemical Kinetics - Test 4", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 30, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0232"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b022f", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0118", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9964"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f994a"], "question": {"text": "For a chemical reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, it was found that concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in 30 min. The average rate of the reaction is ________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (in nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "8274bf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0119"}, {"id": "78d53a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b011a"}, {"id": "adb8d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b011b"}, {"id": "48027d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b011c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b011d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ee2"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following reaction\n\\[\n\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{B} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}\n\\]\nThe time taken for \\(\\mathrm{A}\\) to become \\(1 / 4^{\\text {th }}\\) of its initial concentration is twice the time taken to become \\(1 / 2\\) of the same. Also, when the change of concentration of \\(B\\) is plotted against time, the resulting graph gives a straight line with a negative slope and a positive intercept on the concentration axis.\nThe overall order of the reaction is _______"}, "options": [{"id": "7f2138", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b011e"}, {"id": "350f08", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b011f"}, {"id": "1dd4f8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0120"}, {"id": "a358c4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0121"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0122", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "A flask is filled with equal moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. The half lives of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> respectively and are independent of the initial concentration. The time required for the concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to be four times that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.<br />(Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "487f92", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0123"}, {"id": "401fef", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0124"}, {"id": "d161f0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0125"}, {"id": "d1d068", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0126"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0127", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "Consider a complex reaction taking place in three steps with rate constants $k_1, k_2$ and $k_3$ respectively. The overall rate constant $k$ is given by the expression $k=\\sqrt{\\frac{k_1 k_3}{k_2}}$. If the activation energies of the three steps are 60,30 and $10 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}{ }^{-1}$ respectively, then the overall energy of activation in $\\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$ is $\\ldots\\ldots$ . (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "2acb90", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0128"}, {"id": "37f140", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0129"}, {"id": "515c9a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b012a"}, {"id": "0b7797", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b012b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b012c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478b"], "concepts": ["6162fbd06ed13040ec8535a8"], "question": {"text": "<p>For certain chemical reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>, the rate of formation of product is plotted against the time as shown in the figure. The number of <u><strong>Correct</strong></u> statement/s from the following is _____&nbsp;</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F18517714-57d2-4144-9107-0c75c5fea559-9894870.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p>(A) Over all order of this reaction is one<br />(B) Order of this reaction can&#39;t be determined<br />(C) In region-I and III, the reaction is of first and zero order respectively<br />(D) In region-II, the reaction is of first order<br />(E) In region-II, the order of reaction is in the range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></math>.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c20c66", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b012d"}, {"id": "030b3e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b012e"}, {"id": "fdfb22", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b012f"}, {"id": "29b991", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0130"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0131", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b474c"], "question": {"text": "The number of molecules with energy greater than the threshold energy for a reaction increases five fold by a rise of temperature from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>27</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>42</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. Its energy of activation in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> is _________ (Take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6094</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "925ee9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0132"}, {"id": "10cff1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0133"}, {"id": "94378c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0134"}, {"id": "a52c5a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0135"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0136", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["61ab793e6fe44bfe0fe4ae3c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>AB</mi></math> is an elementary reaction.</p><p>For a certain quantity of reactants, if the volume of the reaction vessel is reduced by a factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the rate of the reaction increases by a factor of _____ . (Round off to the Nearest Integer).</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "f2470c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0137"}, {"id": "9c2434", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0138"}, {"id": "b85741", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0139"}, {"id": "1ad954", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b013a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b013b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e67"], "question": {"text": "A radioactive element has a half life of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn></math> days. The percentage of original activity remaining after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>83</mn></math> days is____(Nearest integer)<br />(Given : antilog <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>333</mn></math>, antilog <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>93</mn></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "9d1007", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b013c"}, {"id": "8949d7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b013d"}, {"id": "4e9dd5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b013e"}, {"id": "d5f8e7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b013f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0140", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9964"], "concepts": ["6117b5e4478ae845c43c5e3e"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> for a reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is decomposed in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn></math> minutes. The time taken for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math> decomposition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is ______ minutes."}, "options": [{"id": "fa40ca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0141"}, {"id": "09ed00", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0142"}, {"id": "38e0fc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0143"}, {"id": "22709f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0144"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0145", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478b"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4743"], "question": {"text": "At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>345</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the half life for the decomposition of a sample of a gaseous compound initially at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math> was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>340</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. When the pressure was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math>, the half life was found to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>170</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The order of the reaction is - [integer answer]"}, "options": [{"id": "b0e1c7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0146"}, {"id": "39d86a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0147"}, {"id": "1f0de0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0148"}, {"id": "f8f284", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0149"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b014a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["6162fb926ed13040ec85077d"], "question": {"text": "<p>The reaction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>NO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NOBr</mi></math>&nbsp;takes place through the mechanism given below</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8652;</mo><mrow/></mover><msub><mi>NOBr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>fast</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NOBr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>NO</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NOBr</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>slow</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>The overall order of the reaction is _____.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2add5b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b014b"}, {"id": "cea597", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b014c"}, {"id": "319307", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b014d"}, {"id": "e56976", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b014e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b014f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8ad4"], "question": {"text": "For the reaction \\(\\mathrm{A} \\rightarrow\\) products.<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FaoMZK6z715FJZicnlLIHHRmDJIDuruHiCXakP09-1Zo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br />The concentration of A at 10 minutes is _______ \\(\\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{~L}^{-1}\\) (nearest integer).<br />The reaction was started with \\(2.5 \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{~L}^{-1}\\) of A."}, "options": [{"id": "7e0f3c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0150"}, {"id": "15f07e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0151"}, {"id": "a77423", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0152"}, {"id": "33cf58", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0153"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0154", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "An exothermic reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> has an activation energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If energy change <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;E</mi></math> during the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math>, then the activation energy for the reverse reaction in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math> is&nbsp;<u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</u> (Integer answer)"}, "options": [{"id": "18303c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0155"}, {"id": "e33b63", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0156"}, {"id": "fac398", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0157"}, {"id": "66d49e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0158"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0159", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478b"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4743"], "question": {"text": "For a reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> the half lives are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> when the concentration of reactant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>=</mo></math> respectively. The order of the reaction is"}, "options": [{"id": "504058", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b015a"}, {"id": "908538", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b015b"}, {"id": "bda23c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b015c"}, {"id": "f8413c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b015d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b015e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b56"], "question": {"text": "During Kinetic study of reaction \\(2 A+B \\rightarrow C+D\\), the following results were obtained :\n\\(\\begin{array}{llll} \n& \\text { A [M] } & \\text { B [M] } & \\text { initial rate of formation of D } \\\\\n\\text { I } & 0.1 & 0.1 & 6.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\\\\n\\text { II } & 0.3 & 0.2 & 7.20 \\times 10^{-2} \\\\\n\\text { III } & 0.3 & 0.4 & 2.88 \\times 10^{-1} \\\\\n\\text { IV } & 0.4 & 0.1 & 2.40 \\times 10^{-2} \\\\\n\\end{array}\\)\nBased on above data, overall order of the reaction is ______"}, "options": [{"id": "83db45", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b015f"}, {"id": "b85e11", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0160"}, {"id": "d7eed8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0161"}, {"id": "942d60", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0162"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0163", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["617aa9ffef3fe65ad8e84c38"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the first order reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole of reactant A gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math> moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> minutes. The half life of the reaction is ...... min. (Round off to the nearest integer).</p><p>[Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>69</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Properties of logarithms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><mi>ln</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>(Round off to the nearest integer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "418777", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0164"}, {"id": "674eaf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0165"}, {"id": "ce8078", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0166"}, {"id": "d543b1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0167"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0168", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b474c"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>aA</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>bB</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>cC</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>dD</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the plot of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math>&nbsp;v/s <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is given below:</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F11cb36a8-269d-413e-8ab6-c6301f5dac27-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 226px; height: 174px;\" /></p><p>The temperature at which the rate constant of the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />(Rounded-off to the nearest integer) [Given : The rat5e constant of the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>.]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9d9eaf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0169"}, {"id": "5018ec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b016a"}, {"id": "4829eb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b016b"}, {"id": "4b2dcf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b016c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b016d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478b"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4743"], "question": {"text": "The half life for the decomposition of gaseous compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>240</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> when the gaseous pressure was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn></math> Torr initially. When the pressure was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn></math> Torr, the half life was found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>. The order of the reaction is _____ (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "be3fba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b016e"}, {"id": "f9b544", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b016f"}, {"id": "4c7523", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0170"}, {"id": "0fcd21", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0171"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0172", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["61489977457fcc27bc16f024"], "question": {"text": "The following data were obtained during the first order thermal decomposition of a gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> at constant volume:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>S. No                 Time/s                 Total pressure/(atm)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math>                        <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>                        <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math>                      <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>115</mn></math>                     <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>28</mn></math></p><p>The rate constant of the reaction is _______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> (nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "321af7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0173"}, {"id": "7e5b8b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0174"}, {"id": "fa1e06", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0175"}, {"id": "d89c5d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0176"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0177", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "During the nuclear explosion, one of the products is <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> with half life of <math><mn>6.93</mn></math> years. If <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> was absorbed in the bones of a newly born baby in place of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> how much time, in years, is required to reduce it by <math><mn>90</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math> if it is not lost metabolically ____________."}, "options": [{"id": "701fb1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0178"}, {"id": "d08700", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b0179"}, {"id": "c58186", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b017a"}, {"id": "cba6c4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efb5dcf815cd79b017b"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8